What are the appropriate steps to take after losing track of one's
pet?

I lose track of mine once in a while, and it's usually the case that
they fell down a trap down without my noticing.  I go down a level or
three and am reunited.

Sometimes, though, they're well and truly gone.  I just lost my dog on
my way up from Mine's End, and I couldn't find him after redescending
all the way to the bottom.  The possibilities that occur to me are:

*  Killed by a physical trap.

*  Stepped on a level teleport trap.

*  Stepped on a polymorph trap.

The last one is a distinct possibility in this case, since I stepped
on a such a trap myself, turning into a nalfeshnee (with the nice
effect of giving me three new pets: two other nalfeshnee and a horned
devil).  But I've scanned all of the lower levels with my telepathy,
and no monsters are identified as the name I gave the dog, which I
hazily remember ought to be the case.

In general, what ought one to do in this case?  In the first case, I
suppose I'd have to scour every level the trap may have occurred on,
checking every corpse to see whether it's the dog.  In the second, I'd
have to check every level I've ever visited.  Neither sounds very fun,
and if the dog was teleported to another level I imagine it'll
probably go feral before I find it.  Should I just give it up for
lost?

